  "finalText": "The 6-second ambient loop is built on the Main composition (1920×1080, 30 fps). Critique scores it 100/100 with no issues.\n\n- **Background:** deep navy-violet `#0b0718`.\n- **Orbs:** four heavily blurred ellipses in purple, violet, fuchsia and teal, named \"Orb cyan\", \"Orb violet\", \"Orb teal\" and \"Orb fuchsia\". Each drifts on a slow sine/cosine path of about 70–110 px.\n- **Dot grid:** one \"Dot grid\" layer of 84 small lavender dots (12×7). It breathes in opacity (about 15–75%) with a slight scale swing (±4%).\n\nThe loop is seamless by construction. Every motion is a sine or cosine with a period of exactly 6 s, driven by expressions rather than keyframes, so frame 0 and frame 6 s match with no closing key needed. The contact sheet at 0, 2, 4 and 6 s shows the expected drift.\n\nI raised the dot opacity after the first check because the dots were barely visible. I haven't re-rendered the contact sheet since that change.\n\nPossible next tweaks: a per-dot ripple across the grid instead of a whole-grid breath, or slower or faster orb drift."
